From 2660a397b4b8624d2ede9db865605f828eb74844 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:39:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 36/44] input: do not wait out the idle interval for the tail
 to finish

At the end of a pass the decoders are drained and the main loop waits for
them to report empty before it will repeat the item. It waited at the
idle rate, a tenth of a second, so the output had already played dry and
sat silent for up to that long before the next pass was even asked for.
Captured from the sink's monitor, that showed as 50-125 ms of silence at
every loop.

Poll at a twentieth of that instead. The wait itself has to stay - it is
what holds playback to real time, since the drain does not finish until
the audio has actually been heard - so only the slack goes.

The gap at each repeat falls to 25 ms, which is the resolution of the
measurement rather than a figure I can stand behind as exact. Playback
rate is unchanged: three repeats of a four second file in a fifteen
second run, and 14.9 s of audio reaching the device, both the same as
before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/input/input.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/input/input.c b/src/input/input.c
index eb30a53409..ab37a7c7e8 100644
--- a/src/input/input.c
+++ b/src/input/input.c
@@ -774,8 +774,12 @@ static void MainLoop( input_thread_t *p_input, bool b_interactive )
             }
             else if( !es_out_GetEmpty( input_priv(p_input)->p_es_out ) )
             {
+                /* Poll for the tail to finish, but not at the idle rate: what
+                 * follows a repeat cannot be asked for until this reports
+                 * empty, so a tenth of a second of slack here is a tenth of a
+                 * second of silence at every loop. */
                 msg_Dbg( p_input, "waiting decoder fifos to empty" );
-                i_wakeup = mdate() + INPUT_IDLE_SLEEP;
+                i_wakeup = mdate() + INPUT_IDLE_SLEEP / 20;
             }
             /* Pause after eof only if the input is pausable.
              * This way we won't trigger timeshifting for nothing */
